  "notes": "A gulper (pelican) eel swimming right: an enormous slit of a mouth (e1, a deep dent) on a tadpole body that thins to a whip tail. The tail tip (e3, the mouth moved back a tile) lies in the open jaws of the eel behind, so each gulper is swallowing the next one's glowing tail organ. TGTG forces the thin tail: the belly's glide image is the back, so a deep head is a thin tail. Its e1 has 5 points (the slit needs a sharp end), so it is not in the koi morph set: its mouth dent and their snout bumps cross when blended.",
